('GZ10','The Cyber Café Saved Your Evening','the-cyber-cafe-saved-your-evening','An early-2000s memory that never happened.','Adult at an old desktop in a small cyber cafe; direct flash, blank CRT display, worn swivel chair and a friend waiting outside.','Retro / Instagram Post','era-transformation','a-frame-from-another-decade','Ordinary retro environment with flash/film cues around a person.','Different venue but no compelling new visual event.','AP02',3,3,3,'reject-generic','Fictional Indian woman, 22, medium-brown complexion, loose ponytail, ordinary build.','4:5',['cinematic'],'Nostalgic props alone are not enough.','Invented screen text, brands and age regression.'),
('GZ11','Three Friends, One Gravity Error','three-friends-one-gravity-error','The common room cannot agree which way is down.','Three friends sit on three separate walls of a college common room, each with a different local gravity. One rotating-room illusion.','Friends','multiple-gravity-set','one-day-four-possible-worlds','Several isolated people/depictions in one composed world, though here identities differ.','New spatial mechanism but competes with GZ01 and creates too much anatomy/identity risk.','CG01',5,4,4,'defer-feasibility','Three fictional Indian adults, 20–25, varied complexions and builds.','4:5',['creative-transformations'],'Not selected; prioritise one stable person in GZ01 and stable group in GZ03.','Independent body orientations and furniture contact likely fail in one generation.'),
('GZ12','Your Memory Becomes a Stamp','your-memory-becomes-a-stamp','A travel moment printed on a giant postage stamp.','A reference travel photo re-rendered as textured ink within perforated paper edges, with no lettering.','Travel / Post','print-transformation','last-train-two-ink-portrait','Face becomes a textured graphic print.','Perforated border does not justify another print concept.','CG03',3,2,3,'reject-duplicate','Fictional Indian adult, 26, natural complexion and proportions.','4:5',['travel'],'No source enamel badge imitation; still rejected against our own print content.','Print simplification and tiny facial features.'),
